WEBVTT

1
00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.400
I won't forget that morning,
not if I left to be a hundred.

2
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.300
I counted the men as they
marched out of the yard.

3
00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.640
They'd hardly slept for weeks.

4
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:07.640
We at the CID had slept even less, but the
nightmare that kept us awake was all the

5
00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:08.900
same nightmare.

6
00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:13.380
That's why we weren't surprised when the
commissioner asked us up to the conference

7
00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:14.880
room for a bit of a talk.

8
00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.180
He'd talked to us plenty, we knew that.

9
00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:20.100
It didn't help any to
know what was ahead of us.

10
00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.780
Must we have that window open, Gregson?

11
00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.700
Oh, shut it if you want to.

12
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:35.080
The chief will be in enough of a temper
without having a ruddy blast down the back

13
00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.180
of his neck.

14
00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.827
Gentlemen, the commissioner.

15
00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:47.940
Stuffy in here.

16
00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.460
Be seated, won't you?

17
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.080
Gentlemen, If you wish to know what able
men you are, read any of the works of

18
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.920
popular fiction that
glamorize your achievements.

19
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.140
But don't I beg of you,
read the daily papers.

20
00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:09.100
They might give you
an inferiority complex.

21
00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.300
I hate to mention it.

22
00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:16.200
But we are confronted with a series of
the most atrocious murders since Jack the

23
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.280
Ripper.

24
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:22.840
And in the meantime, the CID might
as well be playing at Shove-Hatney.

25
00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.120
For all the good we've accomplished.

26
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.620
Now look.

27
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.280
Here, here and here.

28
00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:36.460
Each of these red flags scattered through
the city stands for a woman brutally

29
00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:37.300
murdered.

30
00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.180
A woman's terror, a woman's death agony.

31
00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.280
These are no ordinary crimes.

32
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:47.840
These are the works of a fiend who
kills first and mutilates afterwards.

33
00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:51.980
A ghoul who hacks off a part of his
victim body and carries it away with him.

34
00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.360
a loathsome souvenir of his butchery.

35
00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:00.320
Three women murdered so far,
and you haven't turned in one clue.

36
00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.840
You haven't given me one lead.

37
00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:09.620
Here you sit and wait for news of a
fourth victim with your arms folded.

38
00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.420
Well, we hadn't long to wait.

39
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:19.940
It was down Lambeth Way where a young
woman was hurrying home late last night.

40
00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:21.920
She saw something and stopped.

41
00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.900
It was a constable.

42
00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.880
He spoke to her and he walked
along with her, just in case.

43
00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.280
He saw her down the stairway to the
basement lodging where she lived.

44
00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:38.620
We can only surmise
what happened after that.

45
00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:57.060
Well, I put my pride in my pocket and went
to see the man who so often helped out

46
00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.900
Inspector Lestrade and myself in the past.

47
00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.460
Mr. Sherlock Holmes.

48
00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:12.020
If ever a man needed help, I did.

49
00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.760
This makes four, Inspector.

50
00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.180
Four defenseless women
here in the heart of London.

51
00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.600
And everyone with the
right forefinger hacked off.

52
00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.040
Not hacked, Inspector Gregson.

53
00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.180
Cleanly expertly severed.

54
00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:34.220
The work of a skilled surgeon.

55
00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.920
That's our only clue.

56
00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:38.600
Much about the age of my sister's girl.

57
00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.300
Is there no way of stopping this, Mr.

58
00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.380
Holmes?

59
00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:42.780
Yes.

60
00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.460
There's a way, somehow.

61
00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.520
The fiend that did this.

62
00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.520
I promise.

63
00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.920
I promise. We've nothing to go on.

64
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.200
That's the rotten part of it.

65
00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:56.560
We can't get far without
knowing the motive.

66
00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.140
Well, at least we know
what the motives were not.

67
00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.340
It wasn't robbery.

68
00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.680
No passion, thanks be, nor yet vengeance.

69
00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.960
Because they all came of
totally unrelated families.

70
00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.569
Steady, Inspector. Steady.

71
00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.500
Sorry, Mr. Holmes.

72
00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:11.580
I don't turn a hair when it's a
bloke that can look after himself.

73
00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.760
A little slip of a thing like that.

74
00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.865
Yes, it's horrible.
Come on, let's get a drink.

75
00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.200
Good evening, Mr. Holmes.
Good evening, Vincent.

76
00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.960
Miss Consotto, please, and a double
for my friend here, Inspector Gregson.

77
00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:42.800
There you go, sir.

78
00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:43.940
Eggvine Irish.

79
00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.900
Decent of you to give me
a hand with this thing, Mr.

80
00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:46.480
Holmes.

81
00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.560
Always a pleasure to be of help
to Scotland Yard, Inspector.

82
00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.180
Little out of my house.
Little out of my house.

83
00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:51.480
I'm looking for a maniac.

84
00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:54.320
The murder is just for the fun of a...

85
00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:57.220
Or perhaps just to get a human finger.

86
00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.120
In all four cases,

87
00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.840
the murderer risk capture and
stopping to secure a finger.

88
00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.380
What about four? Who knows?

89
00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:14.160
He's just a madman.

90
00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:16.120
Perhaps there's Mithrid in his madness.

91
00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.200
Yes.

92
00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.980
If we could just trace
those missing fingers.

93
00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:20.920
If.

94
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.360
If we could just drag the English
channel, we might find a penny.

95
00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:24.940
Huh?

96
00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:26.360
Huh. Oh, thank you.

97
00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:29.480
You may get those, Mr Holmes.

98
00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:30.560
Thank you.

99
00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:37.760
Sir George Fenwick, isn't he?

100
00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:38.540
Yes.

101
00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:40.300
Is that his daughter with him?

102
00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:42.320
Don't be so naive, Inspector.

103
00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.980
You know everyone, don't you, darling?

104
00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:47.920
Well, hardly.

105
00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.040
A week ago, I didn't know you.

106
00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.020
A week.

107
00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:52.760
How fast it's got.

108
00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:06.760
I collect these things.

109
00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.520
How very quaint of you.

110
00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.420
Shall we go? Yes.

111
00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:16.140
What are you looking at, Mr.

112
00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.220
Holmes?

113
00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:19.921
Looking at a very handsome woman.

114
00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:23.540
Not want of a purple, but
giving an excellent imitation.

115
00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:25.340
Would you like to come
to my flat for a nightcap?

116
00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.660
Lovely idea. Yes, isn't it?

117
00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.160
I wonder where she's
taking Sir George Fenwick.

118
00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:38.860
Don't be so...

119
00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:40.060
naive, Mr.

120
00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.140
Holmes.

121
00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:56.880
Thank you.

122
00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:38.800
Good evening, Mum. Hello, Crandon.

123
00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:40.460
Any messages? No, Mum.

124
00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:42.160
Thank you.

125
00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:46.240
Uh, drinks, Crandon.

126
00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:47.340
One of your nice surprises.

127
00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:49.380
Yes, Mum. I say, you
don't mean that, uh...

128
00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:51.480
Crandon's a marvel, aren't you, Crandon?

129
00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:52.660
Yes, Mum.

130
00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.489
You wouldn't believe
the things she can do.

131
00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:58.780
Ah, charming place.

132
00:08:58.860 --> 00:08:59.500
Delightful.

133
00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:00.820
Really? You think so?

134
00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:02.100
I'm so glad.

135
00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.140
Lucid, Anne.

136
00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:06.420
Do you mind?

137
00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:08.920
What a question.

138
00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.840
I don't mind anything really.

139
00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:15.160
Except not being with you.

140
00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.400
Now you really don't want
me to believe that do you?

141
00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:19.120
Not too seriously.

142
00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.820
Good. We're both quite grown up aren't we?

143
00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.040
Quite.

144
00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:31.620
You're a treasure Crandon.

145
00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.191
And lower the light a little as you leave.

146
00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.980
I prefer a more flattering light.

147
00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.040
In any light you'd be...

148
00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:51.120
Would I?

149
00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:53.260
And don't you know it.

150
00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.280
Perhaps I do.

151
00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:06.140
Oh, that priceless woman.

152
00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.700
She doesn't believe it,
but she's absurdly romantic.

153
00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:12.020
She loves dreamy music
and she thinks that we...

154
00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:14.320
But we do, don't we?

155
00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:15.400
Do we?

156
00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:19.120
Well, it's rather soothing, restful.

157
00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:20.200
Yes.

158
00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:25.880
And we all need rest at times, like
tired children who've played too long.

159
00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:30.600
You've played with wooden
soldiers, I suppose.

160
00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:31.640
Hmm.

161
00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:34.073
Funny. Hadn't thought of that for years.

162
00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:37.160
The toy boats were my special joy.

163
00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:40.036
Anything I could set afloat anywhere.

164
00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:44.240
Like this and this.

165
00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:48.540
Toy boats sailing into
the Never Never Land.

166
00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:51.180
The land of beautiful dreams.

167
00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:52.920
Look.

168
00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:56.460
Look, isn't it odd how
the light is reflected?

169
00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:01.640
Little specks of light that move and move.

170
00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:05.020
like stars on a slowly moving stream.

171
00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.320
You know, Holmes, I'm very
sensitive to atmosphere.

172
00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:12.280
Oh? Yes, I can tell by the feel of this
room there's been a murder committed here.

173
00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:15.300
It may interest you to know, my dear fellow,
it was the other side of that door at

174
00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.140
the foot of the stairs that
the poor girl was murdered.

175
00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:18.740
If only I could find it.

176
00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:19.820
Find what?

177
00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:24.060
The one thing these unfortunate victims
have in common that might give us a motive

178
00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:25.040
for these murders.

179
00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:27.780
There must be something. I'm the
Jack the Ripper, if you ask me,

180
00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:29.740
a homicidal maniac. No, Watson.

181
00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:34.880
His victims were all from one walk of life
living in the same section of the city.

182
00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:38.400
In this case, the murderer chooses his
victims from all walks of life and from

183
00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:39.780
different sections of the city.

184
00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:43.260
No, my dear fellow, this is not
the work of a homicidal maniac.

185
00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:45.440
It's something infinitely more sinister.

186
00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:47.440
You mean the creeps? What on
earth are you talking about?

187
00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:48.520
Watson,

188
00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:53.100
I'm convinced that these murders are
only incidental to some larger and more

189
00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:56.240
diabolical scheme. That may be,
but why the severed fingers?

190
00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:59.040
The answer to that question, my dear
fellow, is our only hope of solving these

191
00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:00.120
mysteries.

192
00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:04.560
I had such a lovely holiday
at Brighton with you and Alf.

193
00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:07.464
And I'm looking forward
to being with you again.

194
00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:08.980
Poor little thing.

195
00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:11.200
Sort of raises a lump in your throat.

196
00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:14.160
I can picture her sitting here
happily writing this letter.

197
00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:17.534
And not realizing that she's
shortly going to her death.

198
00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:20.580
Hello. Gregson.

199
00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:25.700
Oh, there you are, Mr. Holmes.

200
00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:26.680
I've been looking for you everywhere.

201
00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:30.407
What's happened? Murder in
Edgeway Road, not half an hour ago.

202
00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:32.964
Right forefinger cut off clean.

203
00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:14.860
Fertigy, Edgware, Ruth.

204
00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.080
Meet all the men for murder.

205
00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:19.760
All the murder of a young woman.

206
00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:23.340
Get your papers.

207
00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:28.220
All the murder, paper,
all about the murder.

208
00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:31.160
Morning, paper.

209
00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.760
All about the murder.

210
00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:35.220
Paper, all the murder.

211
00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:39.080
Another young woman
found murder, paper sir.

212
00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:42.320
All the murder, paper, paper.

213
00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.100
Read all about it!

214
00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:48.860
Catch your pipe here!

215
00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:50.440
Murdering Edgeware Road!

216
00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:52.560
Horrible finger murder!

217
00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:57.440
Shocking murder!

218
00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:59.180
Murdering Edgeware Road!

219
00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:02.720
Horrible murder for young women!

220
00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:07.680
Read all about the murder!

221
00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:14.560
Only fancy, Mum.

222
00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:17.100
There's been another of
those horrible murders.

223
00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:18.640
Dear, dear, how shocking.

224
00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:19.820
Yes, Mum.

225
00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.920
I really don't feel
quite safe here myself.

226
00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:25.540
Oh, dear.

227
00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:38.880
Why, Sir George! I must
see Miss Marlow at once.

228
00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:40.260
I don't know if she... I must see her.

229
00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:41.340
Where is she?

230
00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:50.920
I don't know.

231
00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.000
You have to help me.

232
00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.260
But I don't understand.

233
00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:55.280
Listen.

234
00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:57.240
I woke up a few minutes ago

235
00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:00.820
in a cheap boarding
house off Edgware Road.

236
00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:02.220
I don't know how I came there.

237
00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:03.120
I don't know when.

238
00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:04.620
The last thing I remember
is being here with you.

239
00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:06.240
Calm yourself, Sir George.

240
00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:08.120
When did I leave here?

241
00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:10.660
Well, it was about...

242
00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:13.960
It was about... It was 10.45, Mum.

243
00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.180
Precisely.

244
00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:21.200
You seemed, forgive me,
just a little distressed.

245
00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:23.680
Detached, not interested.

246
00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.349
I thought I'd said
something to offend you.

247
00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:28.640
I don't remember.

248
00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.080
I can't remember.

249
00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:39.420
Tell me, has this happened to you before?

250
00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:41.080
Before?

251
00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:48.100
If it was 10.45 when I left you,

252
00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:50.740
it was nine this morning when I woke,

253
00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:53.460
over ten hours lost.

254
00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.419
Ten hours that I can't account for.

255
00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:00.600
And in my pocket when I woke, I found...

256
00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.100
Yeah, in my pocket.

257
00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:06.000
That, that, that isn't...

258
00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:07.740
Oh, it's not for you, of course.

259
00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:08.980
It can't be.

260
00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:14.320
Excuse me, Mum, but there's a
man asking to see the gentleman.

261
00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:16.380
Send him away. Yes, ma'am.

262
00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:18.240
No, no, no, no, please.

263
00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:19.700
I'll see him.

264
00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:28.460
Well?

265
00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:31.020
Delightful room.

266
00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:34.740
Not much like the place
you woke up in this morning.

267
00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:36.260
You followed me here?

268
00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:37.340
Yes.

269
00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:40.780
Are you a detective?

270
00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:41.860
Oh, no.

271
00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:43.980
Quite the contrary.

272
00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.160
Don't be afraid, Sir George.

273
00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:47.720
You know my name?

274
00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:48.720
Oh, yes.

275
00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:51.460
A very old and highly honored name.

276
00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:55.920
And being the bearer of such a
name, and also a very wealthy man,

277
00:16:56.000 --> 00:17:01.000
I thought you might care to
possess yourself with this trifle.

278
00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:05.900
Rather than let it fall
into the hands of the police.

279
00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:07.740
It is yours, if I'm not mistaken.

280
00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:09.380
The initials, G.F.

281
00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:13.960
Where did you get this?

282
00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:16.140
It came out of your pocket.

283
00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:19.400
I saw it fall, but you never noticed.

284
00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:24.180
You were very busy...

285
00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:26.420
bending over something...

286
00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:27.880
with a knife.

287
00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.715
Then you put something in your pocket.

288
00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:44.320
Come along Holmes, come along, come along.

289
00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:45.760
How many more times, must I tell you?

290
00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:47.520
You're missing a treat. This is delicious.

291
00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:49.320
Little jam tarts to follow.

292
00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:50.518
Aren't you tempted?

293
00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:51.620
Mm.

294
00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.640
You and your fleshpots.

295
00:17:57.620 --> 00:18:01.100
They tell me that the fish
is good for the brains.

296
00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:02.940
Brains haven't any.

297
00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:07.220
You realize that a day, a whole day, and
a night have gone by since that best of

298
00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:08.900
affair in Edgewell Road?

299
00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:10.962
I'm as much in the dark as ever.

300
00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:21.392
Hello, here comes a client,
unless I'm very much mistaken.

301
00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:30.740
Well, attractive.

302
00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:32.120
Very attractive.

303
00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:40.500
Obviously she left home under the
stress of some very great emotion.

304
00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:42.700
How do you know that? She
isn't wearing any gloves.

305
00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:44.860
A startling omission on
a young lady of fashion.

306
00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:46.280
No, she didn't put her coat on.

307
00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:47.800
Open car too.

308
00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:55.460
Furthermore, there's something
in that bag she wants to show me.

309
00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:58.180
What makes you say that? The
bag doesn't match her dress,

310
00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:01.560
indicating it was picked
for size rather than style.

311
00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:03.880
It accommodates on bulky object.

312
00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:06.020
You're amazed, Holmes.

313
00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:08.100
Well, I mentioned earlier, fellow.

314
00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:13.980
Oh, that's interesting.

315
00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:15.060
What is?

316
00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:19.260
The cab, turning up the empty house.

317
00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:24.000
I wonder why he followed her here.

318
00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:25.340
Oh, wouldn't you?

319
00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:27.891
All right, Pastor, let me do with glasses.

320
00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.060
Well, we shall soon know.

321
00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:47.440
Yes, Mrs. Hudson?

322
00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:51.700
It's a young lady, sir. Most urgent.

323
00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:54.580
Ask her to come in. Oh, go right in, miss.

324
00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:59.260
Mr. Holmes? Yes, this is my friend, Dr.

325
00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:00.634
Watson. How do you do?

326
00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:01.320
Mr.

327
00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:03.680
Holmes, I... You must excuse me, please.

328
00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.525
Yes, well, won't you sit down?

329
00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.020
Come along. May I?

330
00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:09.000
It's quite all right.

331
00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:10.500
Thank you.

332
00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:21.980
Now try to control yourself,
Miss Fenwick, you're with friends.

333
00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:23.060
You know my name?

334
00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:24.360
No magic, I assure you.

335
00:20:24.440 --> 00:20:26.140
I've often seen your picture.

336
00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:27.800
You're the daughter of Sir
George Fenwick, aren't you?

337
00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:28.660
Yes.

338
00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:30.740
It's about my father that I...

339
00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:33.120
What about your father, Miss Fenwick?

340
00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:35.040
Oh, I don't know what to do.

341
00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:38.500
He's always been the
nicest, dearest person.

342
00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:41.080
Only since Mother died.

343
00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:43.420
Yes, yes, we know.

344
00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:48.995
So I didn't think anything of it when
he was away all night before last.

345
00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:51.000
He didn't come home until
yesterday at tea time.

346
00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:52.980
He didn't come in for dinner at all.

347
00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:56.260
Just paced up and down in
the library hour after hour.

348
00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:58.909
I begged him to let
me in, but he wouldn't.

349
00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.600
Steady, steady.

350
00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:03.200
Now take your time.

351
00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:05.820
I couldn't sleep a wink last night.

352
00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:08.320
Then I started hearing things.

353
00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:10.720
Hearing things? What sort of things?

354
00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:14.260
I heard someone in the
garden underneath my window.

355
00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:18.200
Then I saw a figure moving
down the garden path.

356
00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:20.460
as my father,

357
00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:24.140
stealing through his
own garden like a thief.

358
00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:32.880
He had a spade in his hand, and he stopped
by the greenhouse where he started to

359
00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:33.960
dig.

360
00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:43.060
This morning, at daybreak, I stole
onto the garden and found this.

361
00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:50.860
A finger.

362
00:21:51.020 --> 00:21:52.640
A human finger.

363
00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:54.955
Bring up Scotland Yard, Willie Watson.

364
00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:58.120
Ask him to get hold of Inspector
Gregson and tell him to meet us once.

365
00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:00.435
It's George Phoenix's house, Kingston.

366
00:22:00.600 --> 00:22:02.900
Operator, get Miss Scotland Yard quick.

367
00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:08.740
Where's my father Norris?
He's still in an ivory, Miss.

368
00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:10.080
Thank you. We'll see him right away.

369
00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:11.180
Will you come with me, please?

370
00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:11.960
Thank you.

371
00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:13.340
I got your message, Mr. Holmes.

372
00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:14.420
Yes, indeed.

373
00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:19.500
Dad, may I come in?

374
00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:23.100
Dad!

375
00:22:23.740 --> 00:22:24.920
That's funny.

376
00:22:26.260 --> 00:22:27.820
He doesn't answer.

377
00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:29.620
Do you mind?

378
00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:31.360
Please do. Thank you.

379
00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:34.280
Watson, quick.

380
00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:35.460
Come along, my dear. No, no, no.

381
00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:36.380
Take charge, Miss Fennig, please.

382
00:22:36.460 --> 00:22:37.880
Please, please, please.
Please, please, please.

383
00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:39.078
Come along with me.

384
00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:45.800
Dead?

385
00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:47.140
Yes.

386
00:22:49.820 --> 00:22:51.340
What do you make of it, Doctor?

387
00:22:51.420 --> 00:22:53.820
Shot in the back, between
the second and third ribs.

388
00:22:53.900 --> 00:22:56.140
The bullet undoubtedly
penetrated the heart.

389
00:22:56.220 --> 00:22:57.960
Look at the powder marks on his coat.

390
00:22:58.040 --> 00:22:59.380
I was afraid of this.

391
00:22:59.460 --> 00:23:00.420
What do you mean?

392
00:23:00.500 --> 00:23:03.080
Don't you remember the man in the cab
who followed Miss Finnick to Baker Street?

393
00:23:03.160 --> 00:23:04.660
Well, you don't think he had
anything to do with it, do you?

394
00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:08.720
I think it's reasonable to assume that he
tipped off someone that I'd been sent for.

395
00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:12.440
Sir George has obviously been murdered
to keep him from telling me what he knew.

396
00:23:12.520 --> 00:23:13.991
What was the weapon used?

397
00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:21.020
The murderer came in
through those French windows.

398
00:23:21.100 --> 00:23:24.000
The mud from the garden
he brought in on his boots.

399
00:23:24.080 --> 00:23:26.480
Sir George must have
surprised the intruder.

400
00:23:26.560 --> 00:23:28.280
Passed the room to him here.

401
00:23:30.140 --> 00:23:31.640
The follows we can't tell.

402
00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.760
But from the location of the wound,

403
00:23:33.840 --> 00:23:37.180
I'd say that he turned his back
for a moment, and as he turned,

404
00:23:37.260 --> 00:23:40.940
the muzzle of the revolver was placed
between his ribs, and one muffled shot fired.

405
00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:43.700
And you mean to say he kept on
going, even after he was shot?

406
00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:44.720
There's no doubt about it.

407
00:23:44.800 --> 00:23:45.800
Look there.

408
00:23:46.640 --> 00:23:49.820
The trail of blood leads
us back to the desk.

409
00:23:50.340 --> 00:23:52.280
Something Sir George was after.

410
00:23:54.780 --> 00:23:55.780
Something.

411
00:23:55.980 --> 00:23:58.200
I know. He was trying
to summon help, Poacher.

412
00:23:58.280 --> 00:23:59.320
I don't think so, Watson.

413
00:23:59.400 --> 00:24:01.812
There's the bell pulled by the fireplace.

414
00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:06.660
No, you'll notice from the trail of blood
that Sir George made straight for this

415
00:24:06.740 --> 00:24:08.300
desk here. I wonder.

416
00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:11.556
There was something he was
desperately anxious to get.

417
00:24:12.120 --> 00:24:13.140
Hello. No.

418
00:24:13.380 --> 00:24:15.000
His right hand's clenched.

419
00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:16.720
That's perfectly natural.

420
00:24:16.800 --> 00:24:19.380
Death agony. The left hand lies open.

421
00:24:19.760 --> 00:24:21.800
Why only one hand clenched
in the death agony?

422
00:24:21.880 --> 00:24:24.351
The right hand, the hand nearest the desk.

423
00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:25.740
Please note that.

424
00:24:26.280 --> 00:24:30.540
If Sir George took something off this desk,
something so important that he spilled

425
00:24:30.620 --> 00:24:34.380
his last drop of blood to get
it, I want to know what it is.

426
00:24:46.760 --> 00:24:49.120
It's nothing but an ordinary match folder.

427
00:24:49.200 --> 00:24:51.080
Where does that lead us?

428
00:24:52.240 --> 00:24:54.720
I imagine to something
very important, Gregson.

429
00:24:54.800 --> 00:24:56.660
This match folder's from Pembroke House.

430
00:24:56.740 --> 00:24:57.940
Why shouldn't it be?

431
00:24:58.020 --> 00:24:59.480
He was there, you know.

432
00:24:59.560 --> 00:25:03.020
We saw him yesterday. Yes, but the effort
he made after he was shot to get hold of

433
00:25:03.100 --> 00:25:04.160
this match folder.

434
00:25:05.360 --> 00:25:07.160
It's just possible

435
00:25:07.720 --> 00:25:10.900
that he wanted someone to
remember Pembroke House.

436
00:25:11.700 --> 00:25:12.480
They've wished to recover from the past.

437
00:25:12.560 --> 00:25:16.340
I'd call it to someone who saw him
there, someone who, like ourselves,

438
00:25:16.420 --> 00:25:17.740
saw him with a woman.

439
00:25:34.160 --> 00:25:35.340
Come in.

440
00:25:36.200 --> 00:25:38.920
Oh, Dr. Watson, this came by hand for Mr.

441
00:25:39.000 --> 00:25:40.440
Holmes, not ten minutes ago.

442
00:25:40.520 --> 00:25:42.260
Thank you, Mrs. Hudson.

443
00:25:44.140 --> 00:25:45.640
That would be the report from Mr.

444
00:25:45.720 --> 00:25:46.780
George's bank.

445
00:25:46.940 --> 00:25:48.400
The report from Mr. George?

446
00:25:48.480 --> 00:25:49.580
Oh, really?

447
00:25:49.660 --> 00:25:52.560
Don't you remember his daughter told
us that he'd just closed his account?

448
00:25:52.640 --> 00:25:54.228
Had he looked into it once.

449
00:25:57.980 --> 00:25:58.980
Hmm.

450
00:25:59.700 --> 00:26:04.020
He drew out his entire balance
in cash, nearly 10,000 pounds,

451
00:26:04.100 --> 00:26:06.940
yesterday, just after that
young woman was murdered.

452
00:26:07.020 --> 00:26:08.140
What does that suggest to you, Watson?

453
00:26:08.220 --> 00:26:09.780
But he paid it out to someone.

454
00:26:09.860 --> 00:26:10.700
Precisely.

455
00:26:10.780 --> 00:26:13.780
I smelled a faint,
sweet odor of blackmail.

456
00:26:13.860 --> 00:26:16.800
You don't think he paid it out to someone
who saw him murder the McLean woman?

457
00:26:16.880 --> 00:26:18.060
Sir George never murdered anyone.

458
00:26:18.140 --> 00:26:20.920
But he did have that woman's finger,
and he obviously did have a lot of,

459
00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:22.140
and paid out a lot of cash.

460
00:26:22.220 --> 00:26:25.220
That's the terrifying part
about blackmail, Watson.

461
00:26:25.360 --> 00:26:28.360
The victim is afraid to fight the
accusation no matter how false.

462
00:26:28.440 --> 00:26:34.760
Once the accusation is made, his name is
smeared, and sometimes his life is ruined.

463
00:26:35.700 --> 00:26:38.140
Well, Sir George didn't
commit these murders.

464
00:26:38.220 --> 00:26:39.560
What fiend is it?

465
00:26:39.640 --> 00:26:42.400
I rather think they're not
the work of any one man.

466
00:26:42.480 --> 00:26:46.240
Oh, come, Holmes. You don't expect me to
believe there's a whole organization going

467
00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:49.060
about killing people and
chopping off their fingers.

468
00:26:49.140 --> 00:26:51.140
No, it's possible, quite possible.

469
00:26:51.280 --> 00:26:54.320
Well, whoever's behind all this
thing must be out of his mind.

470
00:26:54.400 --> 00:26:57.100
On the contrary, my dear fellow,
if my assumptions are correct,

471
00:26:57.180 --> 00:27:01.160
this little scheme has behind it the most
brilliant and ruthless intellect the world

472
00:27:01.240 --> 00:27:01.980
has ever known.

473
00:27:02.060 --> 00:27:03.660
You don't mean Professor Moriarty?

474
00:27:03.740 --> 00:27:06.140
I do. Oh, steady, Holmes,
you've got him on the brain.

475
00:27:06.220 --> 00:27:08.632
This is the third time in as many months.

476
00:27:09.980 --> 00:27:11.540
He's dead, you know. Is he?

477
00:27:11.620 --> 00:27:15.580
Is he? You know he is. He was hanged
in Montevideo all over a year ago.

478
00:27:15.660 --> 00:27:18.540
I know that someone was hanged
in Montevideo under that name.

479
00:27:18.620 --> 00:27:23.280
But I'll stake my reputation
that Moriarty is alive and here,

480
00:27:23.360 --> 00:27:25.100
now in London.

481
00:27:28.300 --> 00:27:29.300
Hello?

482
00:27:29.540 --> 00:27:31.440
Yes, Dr. Watson, wait a minute.

483
00:27:31.580 --> 00:27:32.580
You me?

484
00:27:34.840 --> 00:27:36.200
Hello, yes.

485
00:27:36.280 --> 00:27:38.120
This is Dr. Watson speaking.

486
00:27:38.240 --> 00:27:40.320
No, no, I'm afraid I've retired.

487
00:27:40.400 --> 00:27:41.871
I don't practice anymore.

488
00:27:42.260 --> 00:27:43.260
What?

489
00:27:43.960 --> 00:27:46.120
Oh, that's a different thing.

490
00:27:46.240 --> 00:27:47.740
An emergency case.

491
00:27:47.960 --> 00:27:49.140
Well, just a minute.

492
00:27:51.920 --> 00:27:53.540
Yes, well, see it.

493
00:27:53.620 --> 00:27:54.540
She's not moved.

494
00:27:54.620 --> 00:27:55.840
Remember that.

495
00:27:55.940 --> 00:27:57.822
Don't touch it till I get there.

496
00:27:59.420 --> 00:28:01.080
Practicase in the Cardinals Mules.

497
00:28:01.160 --> 00:28:02.200
Heavy woman.

498
00:28:02.340 --> 00:28:03.660
14 stone.

499
00:28:08.400 --> 00:28:09.700
14 stone.

500
00:28:09.780 --> 00:28:14.160
Just the sort of person who would hoist
herself up on a stool to feed the canary.

501
00:28:14.240 --> 00:28:17.720
There ought to be a law against fat
people keeping little dicky birds.

502
00:28:17.800 --> 00:28:18.800
Well,

503
00:28:19.800 --> 00:28:21.840
so long old man. It's not me very long.

504
00:28:21.920 --> 00:28:24.180
Haven't used their bag since
I brought little Amelia.

505
00:28:24.260 --> 00:28:25.880
What's her name in the world?

506
00:28:25.960 --> 00:28:27.720
She grew up to be a
very unattractive child.

507
00:28:27.800 --> 00:28:29.340
Well, who wouldn't
with a name like Amelia?

508
00:28:29.420 --> 00:28:30.420
Amelia.

509
00:28:31.220 --> 00:28:32.220
Amelia.

510
00:28:38.220 --> 00:28:39.220
And I can't

511
00:28:44.480 --> 00:28:46.680
have a hand. A little over.

512
00:28:46.760 --> 00:28:47.860
A little over.

513
00:29:33.100 --> 00:29:36.420
Oh, my God.

514
00:29:42.040 --> 00:29:44.000
Oh, Professor Moriarty.

515
00:29:44.080 --> 00:29:46.315
Not that I wish to appear inquisitive.

516
00:29:46.500 --> 00:29:49.040
Not to what am I indebted for
the pleasure of this visit.

517
00:29:49.120 --> 00:29:51.061
Scotland Yard will be interested.

518
00:29:51.420 --> 00:29:55.000
It's very convenient for me to have
Scotland Yard think that I'm still dead in

519
00:29:55.080 --> 00:29:56.180
Montevideo.

520
00:29:57.260 --> 00:29:58.920
I've never dreamed of fooling you.

521
00:29:59.000 --> 00:29:59.760
Thank you.

522
00:29:59.840 --> 00:30:01.780
The thought occurs to me, Mr.

523
00:30:01.860 --> 00:30:05.680
Holmes, that there are some
advantages in living within the law.

524
00:30:07.920 --> 00:30:10.744
You are very comfortably
fixed here, aren't you?

525
00:30:11.640 --> 00:30:17.340
As I get on in life, the little
comforts appeal to me more and more.

526
00:30:17.860 --> 00:30:18.860
Oh, I beg your pardon.

527
00:30:18.940 --> 00:30:20.100
Won't you sit down?

528
00:30:21.580 --> 00:30:22.720
Thank you.

529
00:30:36.240 --> 00:30:38.520
And now, Professor Moriarty,
what can I do for you?

530
00:30:38.600 --> 00:30:42.541
Everything that I have to say to
you has already crossed your mind.

531
00:30:42.980 --> 00:30:45.320
And my answer is no doubt crossed yours.

532
00:30:45.400 --> 00:30:46.520
Yes, final.

533
00:30:47.500 --> 00:30:48.720
What do you think?

534
00:30:49.500 --> 00:30:53.088
I shall not rest until you are
hanged for the finger murders.

535
00:30:53.900 --> 00:30:55.600
You have no proof, you know.

536
00:30:59.540 --> 00:31:00.860
You're not a shred.

537
00:31:01.580 --> 00:31:02.900
But I have you.

538
00:31:03.380 --> 00:31:05.920
I can tell you. I would turn you
over to the police here and now.

539
00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:07.120
You could.

540
00:31:07.340 --> 00:31:09.920
But if you did, you'd never see Dr.

541
00:31:10.000 --> 00:31:11.060
Watson again.

542
00:31:11.300 --> 00:31:13.000
Oh, the telephone call.

543
00:31:13.320 --> 00:31:14.100
Quite.

544
00:31:14.180 --> 00:31:17.300
I rather assumed you had
taken some such precaution,

545
00:31:18.160 --> 00:31:23.040
or I should have snatched up a revolver
and indulged in a fit of heroics when you

546
00:31:23.120 --> 00:31:25.380
came in. Very smart, aren't you?

547
00:31:26.940 --> 00:31:28.500
Not smart enough.

548
00:31:28.760 --> 00:31:30.300
Or I should have anticipated you.

549
00:31:30.380 --> 00:31:31.380
But...

550
00:31:34.980 --> 00:31:37.400
I shall not rest until I
find you, and when I do...

551
00:31:37.480 --> 00:31:40.060
No harm will come to Dr. Watson this time.

552
00:31:40.480 --> 00:31:42.600
But I can't answer for the future.

553
00:31:43.060 --> 00:31:46.460
Mr. Holmes, I should strongly
advise you to drop this case.

554
00:31:46.540 --> 00:31:47.860
Don't be silly.

555
00:31:47.940 --> 00:31:48.960
Think it over.

556
00:31:49.220 --> 00:31:51.340
We've had many encounters in the past.

557
00:31:51.420 --> 00:31:53.280
You hope to place me on the gallows.

558
00:31:53.360 --> 00:31:56.301
I tell you, I shall never
stand up on the gallows.

559
00:31:57.160 --> 00:32:01.260
But, if you are instrumental in any
way in bringing about my destruction,

560
00:32:01.340 --> 00:32:04.680
you will not be alive to
enjoy your satisfaction.

561
00:32:04.980 --> 00:32:07.200
walk together through the
gates of eternity hand in hand.

562
00:32:07.280 --> 00:32:08.700
What a charming picture that would make.

563
00:32:08.780 --> 00:32:11.956
Yes, wouldn't it? I really
think it might be worth it.

564
00:32:18.060 --> 00:32:18.860
Shoelaces, Governor?

565
00:32:18.940 --> 00:32:20.060
Tons of pay.

566
00:32:20.280 --> 00:32:21.960
And strong enough to end yourself.

567
00:32:22.040 --> 00:32:24.900
How many more times since I tell you I
don't want your filthy shoelaces or your

568
00:32:24.980 --> 00:32:25.980
company?

569
00:32:27.820 --> 00:32:29.540
Shoelaces, Governor? Last is impertinence.

570
00:32:29.620 --> 00:32:31.840
Run along with my good man
or I'll give you in charge.

571
00:32:31.920 --> 00:32:33.096
Shoelaces, Governor?

572
00:32:37.380 --> 00:32:38.498
Shoelaces, Captain.

573
00:32:38.780 --> 00:32:40.240
You poor bloke.

574
00:32:40.320 --> 00:32:42.060
What's only got one arm?

575
00:32:42.560 --> 00:32:44.060
Any luck with Mr. Holmes?

576
00:32:44.140 --> 00:32:46.905
You can read his obituary
in tomorrow's papers.

577
00:32:57.440 --> 00:32:59.420
Oh, there you are Watson, come in.

578
00:32:59.500 --> 00:33:00.520
How's that?

579
00:33:01.440 --> 00:33:02.620
Just going out to look for you.

580
00:33:02.700 --> 00:33:04.320
Look for me, what for?

581
00:33:04.820 --> 00:33:06.720
Suppose you don't think
I know my way about?

582
00:33:06.800 --> 00:33:08.100
Well, you're right, I don't.

583
00:33:08.180 --> 00:33:09.960
Blast all practical jokers anyhow.

584
00:33:10.040 --> 00:33:11.200
Know where I've been?

585
00:33:11.280 --> 00:33:13.380
On a wild goose chase. Exactly.

586
00:33:13.520 --> 00:33:15.820
There's no such number in McArdle's muse.

587
00:33:15.900 --> 00:33:17.920
Some fool's idea of a joke.

588
00:33:18.360 --> 00:33:20.200
Did you, uh...

589
00:33:20.560 --> 00:33:22.880
Did you see anyone? No, nobody especially.

590
00:33:22.960 --> 00:33:25.520
Only a whining old
idiot selling bootlaces.

591
00:33:25.600 --> 00:33:26.900
Persistent, beggar, wasn't he?

592
00:33:26.980 --> 00:33:28.540
Stuck to you like grim death.

593
00:33:28.620 --> 00:33:29.660
How do you know?

594
00:33:29.740 --> 00:33:33.600
And finally I left you for someone
who looked like better pickings.

595
00:33:33.680 --> 00:33:36.620
Someone, my dear Watson,
was Professor Moriarty himself.

596
00:33:36.700 --> 00:33:38.480
What? He's just called on me.

597
00:33:38.560 --> 00:33:39.860
Moriarty here and you let him go?

598
00:33:39.940 --> 00:33:41.460
But you must be out of your mind.

599
00:33:41.540 --> 00:33:42.220
Why?

600
00:33:42.300 --> 00:33:45.200
Well, he bluffed me into believing that he
was holding a friend of mine as hostage.

601
00:33:45.280 --> 00:33:46.260
Friend of yours who?

602
00:33:46.340 --> 00:33:48.300
Oh, nobody very important,
just a fat lazy fellow.

603
00:33:48.380 --> 00:33:49.920
Medical man, I believe. Medical man?

604
00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:51.620
Do I know him? Yes, I think you do.

605
00:33:51.700 --> 00:33:52.680
A fellow by the name of Watson.

606
00:33:52.760 --> 00:33:54.525
Watson, Watson, never heard...

607
00:33:54.720 --> 00:33:57.500
Who? Me? I'm afraid so, old fellow.

608
00:33:58.080 --> 00:34:00.360
Your street hawker's job...

609
00:34:01.160 --> 00:34:04.660
I was to do away with you
in a certain contingency.

610
00:34:04.740 --> 00:34:07.200
You let Moriarty go because of me?

611
00:34:07.280 --> 00:34:08.500
I had no choice.

612
00:34:08.600 --> 00:34:10.560
I can't afford to lose you old fellow.

613
00:34:10.640 --> 00:34:13.993
Well, it's very decent of the
old chap I must say, but...

614
00:34:14.920 --> 00:34:16.720
Well, I wish you'd nabbed him.

615
00:34:16.800 --> 00:34:18.240
We shall, never fear.

616
00:34:18.860 --> 00:34:20.800
I know the motive for the finger murders.

617
00:34:20.880 --> 00:34:24.340
All I have to find out now is the
method used with the blackmail victims.

618
00:34:24.420 --> 00:34:25.240
Method?

619
00:34:25.320 --> 00:34:26.280
Yes.

620
00:34:26.360 --> 00:34:29.478
How does Moriarty get them
to the scene of the crime?

621
00:34:29.860 --> 00:34:32.340
Why did he plant those
severed fingers on them?

622
00:34:32.420 --> 00:34:35.340
And how does he scare
them into believing that...

623
00:34:36.440 --> 00:34:39.911
they may have committed those
atrocious murders themselves?

624
00:34:41.100 --> 00:34:42.200
Curious.

625
00:34:46.700 --> 00:34:48.260
Very curious.

626
00:34:49.740 --> 00:34:51.600
Curious? What's curious?

627
00:34:52.940 --> 00:34:56.560
That window in the empty
house across the street.

628
00:34:58.540 --> 00:34:59.980
First floor front.

629
00:35:01.020 --> 00:35:02.120
What's wrong with it?

630
00:35:02.200 --> 00:35:03.200
It's open.

631
00:35:03.440 --> 00:35:05.020
Why shouldn't it be open?

632
00:35:05.200 --> 00:35:06.540
Well, it wasn't open half an hour ago.

633
00:35:06.620 --> 00:35:07.520
I'll stake my life on that.

634
00:35:07.600 --> 00:35:09.180
Well, it's not our business.

635
00:35:09.260 --> 00:35:10.740
Let it stay open.

636
00:35:10.900 --> 00:35:12.000
I, uh,

637
00:35:12.400 --> 00:35:15.260
wonder if you'd go over, old
fellow, and see what's the matter.

638
00:35:15.340 --> 00:35:16.140
Trespassing.

639
00:35:16.220 --> 00:35:17.420
Against the law.

640
00:35:17.500 --> 00:35:18.800
Very well, I'll go myself.

641
00:35:18.880 --> 00:35:20.980
Oh, well, if you're
going to put it like that.

642
00:35:21.060 --> 00:35:25.825
Ridiculous waste of time. Going about
shutting windows at this hour of the night.

643
00:35:26.060 --> 00:35:27.560
I don't want to...

644
00:35:27.780 --> 00:35:29.120
Dignified job for a doctor.

645
00:35:29.200 --> 00:35:30.720
Dr. Watson, the torchbearer.

646
00:35:30.800 --> 00:35:32.040
And what do you propose to do?

647
00:35:32.120 --> 00:35:34.080
Sit in a comfortable chair,
I suppose, and read a good book.

648
00:35:34.160 --> 00:35:36.160
That's a very good idea.
Yeah, that's a very good idea.

649
00:35:36.240 --> 00:35:39.240
While I play night watchman,
you have a nice read.

650
00:35:39.700 --> 00:35:40.720
Good night. Have a good time.

651
00:35:40.800 --> 00:35:41.880
Have a good time.

652
00:35:55.680 --> 00:35:57.080
I don't know anything.

653
00:36:06.720 --> 00:36:08.400
What on earth is this for?

654
00:36:09.620 --> 00:36:10.620
Who?

655
00:36:11.560 --> 00:36:12.860
A Beristairn.

656
00:36:12.960 --> 00:36:15.548
Pretty little thing to
keep about the house.

657
00:36:15.720 --> 00:36:17.160
Must have been a pet.

658
00:36:43.080 --> 00:36:44.340
What's that?

659
00:36:49.220 --> 00:36:51.240
Oh crap, Barbara.

660
00:36:52.560 --> 00:36:54.560
This was a good look.

661
00:37:12.220 --> 00:37:15.620
Well, he sits comfortably reading a book.

662
00:37:45.900 --> 00:37:48.400
He killed Holmes! He killed Sherlock!

663
00:37:48.860 --> 00:37:49.860
Watson.

664
00:37:50.420 --> 00:37:52.640
You? But I saw him shoot you a second ago!

665
00:37:52.720 --> 00:37:54.040
Not me, my dear fellow.

666
00:37:54.120 --> 00:37:56.020
Merely the bust of Julius Caesar.

667
00:37:56.100 --> 00:37:58.700
Incidentally, you may have
noticed that all through the ages,

668
00:37:58.780 --> 00:38:01.720
prominent men have prominent noses.

669
00:38:05.640 --> 00:38:06.640
Oh,

670
00:38:06.900 --> 00:38:08.680
afraid we're in for terrible
trouble again with Mrs.

671
00:38:08.760 --> 00:38:11.580
Hudson. Windows smashed,
plaster all over the floor.

672
00:38:11.660 --> 00:38:12.680
Get up, you.

673
00:38:17.160 --> 00:38:19.500
Corporal Williams, Middlesex Regiment.

674
00:38:19.580 --> 00:38:22.320
Discharge from the Army
is physically unfit.

675
00:38:22.900 --> 00:38:24.520
Papers seem in order.

676
00:38:28.660 --> 00:38:30.140
Now, Corporal Williams,

677
00:38:30.420 --> 00:38:33.160
you've seen service in
the Far East, haven't you?

678
00:38:33.240 --> 00:38:34.600
The East.

679
00:38:34.680 --> 00:38:37.220
I thought so. Look at
his complexion, Watson.

680
00:38:37.300 --> 00:38:39.660
Yellow saffron. He's been taking atabrine.

681
00:38:39.740 --> 00:38:41.240
Cure for malaria.

682
00:38:41.460 --> 00:38:42.680
Sniper, aren't you?

683
00:38:43.720 --> 00:38:44.740
Sniper.

684
00:38:46.580 --> 00:38:48.460
Why did you try to kill me?

685
00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:52.040
I had to kill him.

686
00:38:52.120 --> 00:38:53.660
I had to.

687
00:38:53.740 --> 00:38:55.500
Oh, snap out of it! Stop it, Watson.

688
00:38:55.580 --> 00:38:57.227
He's shamming. No, he isn't.

689
00:38:57.680 --> 00:38:59.480
Who told you to kill me?

690
00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:02.280
She told me.

691
00:39:02.360 --> 00:39:03.480
She told you?

692
00:39:04.060 --> 00:39:07.500
She told me I couldn't miss.

693
00:39:07.580 --> 00:39:09.100
Well, luckily you did miss, you murderer.

694
00:39:09.180 --> 00:39:10.827
He isn't a murderer, Watson.

695
00:39:12.880 --> 00:39:14.409
Listen, Corporal Williams.

696
00:39:15.600 --> 00:39:18.420
She told you you had to do it, didn't she?

697
00:39:19.740 --> 00:39:21.500
I had to do it.

698
00:39:21.580 --> 00:39:22.740
I've got Watson, I've got it.

699
00:39:22.820 --> 00:39:25.300
Got what? The method used
in the finger murders.

700
00:39:25.380 --> 00:39:26.520
Well, what is it?

701
00:39:26.600 --> 00:39:29.040
Hypnotism, my dear fellow, hypnotism.

702
00:39:31.040 --> 00:39:33.840
And it wasn't against his nature,
that's the devilish part of it.

703
00:39:33.920 --> 00:39:37.160
They picked a man for their
purpose whose job was sniping.

704
00:39:37.240 --> 00:39:38.220
Who are they?

705
00:39:38.300 --> 00:39:40.600
Professor Moriarty and
his finger murderers?

706
00:39:40.680 --> 00:39:42.220
William spoke of a woman.

707
00:39:42.780 --> 00:39:46.662
I think you will find that she
asked him home tonight for a drink.

708
00:39:47.220 --> 00:39:50.620
Nice quiet rooms, soft lights, music.

709
00:39:50.700 --> 00:39:51.960
He's got it all packed, Mr.

710
00:39:52.040 --> 00:39:52.680
Holmes.

711
00:39:52.760 --> 00:39:54.220
What's the lady look like?

712
00:39:54.300 --> 00:39:55.300
Oh,

713
00:39:55.500 --> 00:39:59.160
up 30, nice figure, blonde, lustrous eyes.

714
00:39:59.240 --> 00:39:59.860
Oh, really?

715
00:39:59.940 --> 00:40:01.200
Got her phone number?

716
00:40:02.320 --> 00:40:03.580
Oh, sir.

717
00:40:05.280 --> 00:40:07.280
Williams will give us her address.

718
00:40:07.980 --> 00:40:09.380
Look after him, Gregson.

719
00:40:09.460 --> 00:40:11.284
Don't let anyone come near him.

720
00:40:11.720 --> 00:40:13.580
He's our key witness
in the finger murders.

721
00:40:13.660 --> 00:40:15.540
Well, I hope you're guessing right, Mr.

722
00:40:15.620 --> 00:40:16.620
Holmes.

723
00:40:17.200 --> 00:40:18.280
Get up, Williams.

724
00:40:21.020 --> 00:40:23.760
Now, go with Inspector Gregson,
anywhere he tells you.

725
00:40:23.840 --> 00:40:24.840
Come on.

726
00:40:28.040 --> 00:40:29.040
Here.

727
00:40:30.360 --> 00:40:31.920
Ring me as soon as he
comes to himself, will you?

728
00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:33.000
I will.

729
00:40:33.460 --> 00:40:35.460
Good night, gentlemen. Good night.

730
00:40:37.020 --> 00:40:39.160
Well, if you believe that
fellow Williams was hypnotized,

731
00:40:39.240 --> 00:40:41.660
I suppose you think Sir George
Fenwick was hypnotized too.

732
00:40:41.740 --> 00:40:42.920
Yes, I'm quite sure of it.

733
00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:44.340
Have a cup of tea. Thanks, sir boy.

734
00:40:44.420 --> 00:40:45.280
Nothing to eat.

735
00:40:45.360 --> 00:40:48.620
Why didn't these people make
Sir George do the murder himself?

736
00:40:48.700 --> 00:40:51.229
Because they didn't
want to get him hanged.

737
00:40:52.360 --> 00:40:54.580
They, uh... They wanted to blackmail him.

738
00:40:54.660 --> 00:40:57.120
Well, who do you think
the actual murderer is?

739
00:40:57.200 --> 00:40:58.700
Well, Moriarty's gang,

740
00:40:59.020 --> 00:41:01.120
a diabolically simple technique.

741
00:41:01.520 --> 00:41:05.360
Kill a woman... Yes, yes, yes,
but why cut off the fingers?

742
00:41:05.680 --> 00:41:06.960
My dear fellow, don't you understand?

743
00:41:07.040 --> 00:41:10.740
The severed finger is what links
the blackmail victim to the murder.

744
00:41:10.820 --> 00:41:14.100
He wakes, finds the
grizzly thing in his pocket.

745
00:41:14.320 --> 00:41:15.480
Doesn't know how he got there.

746
00:41:15.560 --> 00:41:16.960
He's no idea that he's been hypnotized.

747
00:41:17.040 --> 00:41:21.260
For all he knows, he may have
committed the atrocious crime

748
00:41:21.500 --> 00:41:24.320
during some dreadful lapse of sanity.

749
00:41:24.700 --> 00:41:28.380
In that state when he's utterly
demoralized, the blackmailers take over,

750
00:41:28.460 --> 00:41:31.860
is that it? Undoubtedly. You see, they
swear that they saw him commit the murder.

751
00:41:31.940 --> 00:41:36.705
And being human, the victim will pay
anything rather than stand trial on a charge

752
00:41:37.040 --> 00:41:40.920
I'm loathsome. Well, it all fits
in, if you believe in hypnotism.

753
00:41:41.080 --> 00:41:42.980
The only possible explanation.

754
00:41:43.100 --> 00:41:46.800
You think the hypnotist is
that woman with the blonde hair,

755
00:41:46.880 --> 00:41:49.660
the lustrous eyes, the woman you invented?

756
00:41:49.740 --> 00:41:52.120
I didn't invent her. I saw her.

757
00:41:52.500 --> 00:41:54.020
What are you talking about?

758
00:41:54.100 --> 00:41:55.920
That woman, my dear Watson,

759
00:41:57.100 --> 00:41:59.940
was with Sir George when
he left Pembroke House.

760
00:42:00.020 --> 00:42:04.280
I saw her there. I shall see her again,
and Williams will lead me to her.

761
00:42:04.360 --> 00:42:06.460
That's why it's so
important to keep him safe.

762
00:42:06.540 --> 00:42:08.320
He will identify her.

763
00:42:13.320 --> 00:42:14.600
Hello? Yes?

764
00:42:14.680 --> 00:42:16.000
Inspector Brakeson?

765
00:42:18.500 --> 00:42:19.500
What?

766
00:42:20.220 --> 00:42:22.691
Well, get every constable in the district.

767
00:42:22.800 --> 00:42:24.240
Yes, I'll be over at once.

768
00:42:24.320 --> 00:42:25.820
What's happened, Holmes?
Williams is missing.

769
00:42:25.900 --> 00:42:27.620
Great Scott! Come on.

770
00:42:32.100 --> 00:42:34.900
The lorry crashed into
Braxton's car during confusion.

771
00:42:34.980 --> 00:42:35.900
Williams disappeared.

772
00:42:35.980 --> 00:42:37.900
Escaped him? No. Kidnapped.

773
00:42:37.980 --> 00:42:39.300
To keep him from talking when he came to.

774
00:42:39.380 --> 00:42:40.680
You don't think that Moriarty...

775
00:42:40.760 --> 00:42:41.760
Moriarty?

776
00:42:41.840 --> 00:42:43.320
Anything is possible.

777
00:42:48.100 --> 00:42:49.120
Williams!

778
00:42:49.500 --> 00:42:50.460
Dead.

779
00:42:50.540 --> 00:42:51.780
You see?

780
00:42:51.860 --> 00:42:53.440
Anything is possible.

781
00:43:16.260 --> 00:43:18.920
Good morning, Professor Moriarty.

782
00:43:19.000 --> 00:43:20.400
You startled me.

783
00:43:20.780 --> 00:43:22.720
I'm dressing another dolly.

784
00:43:22.800 --> 00:43:25.080
A dear little nurse.

785
00:43:26.450 --> 00:43:29.300
Is there anything wrong with your finger?

786
00:43:29.380 --> 00:43:30.640
Just a splinter.

787
00:43:30.720 --> 00:43:32.580
Nasty things splinters.

788
00:43:32.660 --> 00:43:34.160
Most trying.

789
00:43:34.240 --> 00:43:36.360
One can't be too careful.

790
00:43:36.440 --> 00:43:38.840
But I'll get it out for you.

791
00:43:38.920 --> 00:43:42.940
I have the very instrument to help you.

792
00:43:45.240 --> 00:43:47.300
They're all sharp enough to split a hair.

793
00:43:47.380 --> 00:43:49.200
Put those tools away until they're needed.

794
00:43:49.280 --> 00:43:51.120
But they're not tools, sir.

795
00:43:51.200 --> 00:43:52.320
They're instruments.

796
00:43:52.400 --> 00:43:53.480
Put them away.

797
00:43:53.620 --> 00:43:54.980
Is Lydia in?

798
00:43:55.060 --> 00:43:56.060
Yes.

799
00:43:57.420 --> 00:44:00.940
But really you should let me...

800
00:44:01.500 --> 00:44:02.820
Get dressed.

801
00:44:03.160 --> 00:44:05.940
Holmes and Watson just left
Baker Street for the Mesmer Club.

802
00:44:06.020 --> 00:44:09.740
Mesmer Club? The meeting place of
all the top hypnotists in London.

803
00:44:09.820 --> 00:44:12.820
Do you suppose that Mr.
Holmes is on to our method?

804
00:44:14.440 --> 00:44:19.060
It's our business to
see that it ends there.

805
00:44:19.140 --> 00:44:20.640
I hope you're right.

806
00:44:20.800 --> 00:44:24.035
William has passed away
before he could talk, remember?

807
00:44:24.460 --> 00:44:26.020
What do you want me to do?

808
00:44:26.100 --> 00:44:30.500
Go to the Mesmer Club, meet Holmes,
and induce him to come back here.

809
00:44:31.640 --> 00:44:33.360
Isn't that a bit dangerous?

810
00:44:33.840 --> 00:44:37.369
Every meeting with Sherlock
Holmes is potentially dangerous.

811
00:44:38.160 --> 00:44:41.631
However, you say he didn't see
your face at Pembroke House.

812
00:44:41.900 --> 00:44:43.360
And how would you suggest that he was?

813
00:44:43.440 --> 00:44:45.700
I get Mr. Holmes to accompany me here.

814
00:44:46.540 --> 00:44:47.360
Kidnap him.

815
00:44:47.440 --> 00:44:48.440
Oh, no.

816
00:44:48.800 --> 00:44:50.200
Holmes has one weakness.

817
00:44:50.280 --> 00:44:52.120
His insatiable curiosity.

818
00:44:52.400 --> 00:44:55.160
If you can arouse that,
you can lead him anywhere.

819
00:44:55.240 --> 00:44:59.181
It's up to you to take advantage
of any opportunity that may arise.

820
00:44:59.660 --> 00:45:01.340
This way, please, gentlemen.

821
00:45:01.780 --> 00:45:03.580
I'll tell Dr. Onslow that you're here.

822
00:45:03.660 --> 00:45:04.660
Thank you.

823
00:45:05.360 --> 00:45:07.120
This is the Mesmer Club.

824
00:45:08.180 --> 00:45:12.160
If you ask me, hypnotism
is a lot of mumbo jumbo.

825
00:45:13.440 --> 00:45:15.680
must admit that hypnotism has
its place in modern science.

826
00:45:15.760 --> 00:45:19.740
That may be, but 90% of hypnotists
and crooks are the worst kind.

827
00:45:19.820 --> 00:45:23.560
Nothing more than a lot of charlatans
exploiting weak-willed morons.

828
00:45:23.640 --> 00:45:25.140
Ah, Dr. Anslow, I believe.

829
00:45:25.220 --> 00:45:26.300
Ah, happy to meet you, Mr.

830
00:45:26.380 --> 00:45:26.880
Holmes.

831
00:45:26.900 --> 00:45:30.000
Your brother Mycroft suggested
I might be of help to you.

832
00:45:30.080 --> 00:45:34.780
He's a valued member of our little
group of charlatans and crooks.

833
00:45:34.860 --> 00:45:35.780
Oh, I beg your pardon, sir.

834
00:45:35.860 --> 00:45:36.660
I didn't know you were listening.

835
00:45:36.740 --> 00:45:38.260
Behind the curtain. My friend, Dr.

836
00:45:38.340 --> 00:45:39.920
Watson. Ah, delighted. Oh, did you?

837
00:45:40.000 --> 00:45:44.000
I wonder now. You see, we're in the midst
of a little experimental session at this

838
00:45:44.080 --> 00:45:47.300
very moment, if you'd care to join us.

839
00:45:47.380 --> 00:45:49.400
Oh, certainly, certainly.
I'll be very instructive.

840
00:45:49.480 --> 00:45:50.920
Oh, well, will you follow me?

841
00:45:51.000 --> 00:45:52.000
Thank you.

842
00:45:53.360 --> 00:45:55.240
...in treating his patients.

843
00:45:55.420 --> 00:46:00.040
But today the therapeutic value
of hypnotism, as we now call it,

844
00:46:00.120 --> 00:46:02.820
is conceded by innumerable physicians.

845
00:46:03.260 --> 00:46:08.020
Especially is it of value in surgical cases
where the administration of local or of

846
00:46:08.100 --> 00:46:10.720
general anaesthetic is inadvisable.

847
00:46:10.880 --> 00:46:12.440
The wiseable poppycock.

848
00:46:12.950 --> 00:46:17.700
For the sake of latecomers, I may say that
I have placed this subject under profound

849
00:46:17.780 --> 00:46:18.740
hypnosis.

850
00:46:18.820 --> 00:46:23.820
In this condition, he can feel no pain,
even under applications which normally would

851
00:46:23.900 --> 00:46:25.220
be excruciating.

852
00:46:25.300 --> 00:46:26.200
Excruciating?

853
00:46:26.280 --> 00:46:28.020
Will you excuse me, please?

854
00:46:29.660 --> 00:46:32.480
Carter, you are having a peaceful sleep.

855
00:46:32.560 --> 00:46:33.860
You feel nothing.

856
00:46:34.350 --> 00:46:37.580
Your arms and your hands
are without sensation.

857
00:46:38.260 --> 00:46:39.840
Mowbray, the long needle.

858
00:46:46.500 --> 00:46:48.382
Carter, give me your right hand.

859
00:46:56.900 --> 00:47:01.160
As you observe, the needle has been thrust
completely through the subject's hand.

860
00:47:01.240 --> 00:47:03.140
No feeling, no pain.

861
00:47:03.220 --> 00:47:08.580
This lack of feeling is the one
infallible test of profound hypnosis.

862
00:47:08.660 --> 00:47:09.500
Nonsense.

863
00:47:09.580 --> 00:47:11.168
The fellow's full of drugs.

864
00:47:11.380 --> 00:47:13.980
Well, isn't he? Definitely not, Doctor.

865
00:47:17.800 --> 00:47:19.620
Wake up Carter, wake up.

866
00:47:19.800 --> 00:47:22.880
You'll feel well and rested
remember, no pain anywhere.

867
00:47:22.960 --> 00:47:24.320
Wake up, wake up.

868
00:47:27.420 --> 00:47:28.820
I say when you're going to begin?

869
00:47:28.900 --> 00:47:30.606
All through Carter, stand up.

870
00:47:33.900 --> 00:47:35.260
This way sir.

871
00:47:36.580 --> 00:47:39.060
And are these all the
people that come here?

872
00:47:39.140 --> 00:47:41.820
Oh no, no, no. Others keep
dropping in all the time.

873
00:47:41.900 --> 00:47:45.000
I suppose it's alright for those who believe
in it, but of course I'm a professional

874
00:47:45.080 --> 00:47:46.260
man myself.

875
00:47:46.400 --> 00:47:48.380
You don't believe in hypnotism, Dr.

876
00:47:48.460 --> 00:47:51.720
Watson. I don't deny that there
are certain types of hysterical,

877
00:47:51.800 --> 00:47:54.600
feeble-minded people who go under
a few point of finger at them.

878
00:47:54.680 --> 00:47:57.640
But anyone with an ounce of character...

879
00:47:57.720 --> 00:47:59.360
How right you are.

880
00:47:59.440 --> 00:48:02.600
You see right through our
little artifices, don't you, Dr.

881
00:48:02.680 --> 00:48:03.780
Watson? Right through, my dear sir.

882
00:48:03.860 --> 00:48:05.480
Right through. Right, sir.

883
00:48:05.740 --> 00:48:09.140
But with the feeble-minded, as you say...

884
00:48:09.220 --> 00:48:10.500
Excuse us, Mr.

885
00:48:10.580 --> 00:48:12.560
Holmes. Oh, certainly.
Step over here, won't you?

886
00:48:12.640 --> 00:48:14.040
Certainly, sir. I don't need to oblige.

887
00:48:14.120 --> 00:48:20.160
Let me show you how easily we
charlatans take advantage of them.

888
00:48:20.240 --> 00:48:22.080
Now, sit down, Doctor.

889
00:48:25.180 --> 00:48:28.460
Now, we set a thing like this in motion.

890
00:48:31.000 --> 00:48:33.600
It's wonderful, the attraction.

891
00:48:33.680 --> 00:48:35.960
On the feeble-minded, of course.

892
00:48:36.040 --> 00:48:38.580
The continuous motion,

893
00:48:38.960 --> 00:48:41.740
if they just let themselves follow it.

894
00:48:41.820 --> 00:48:46.420
Of course, you could stare
at it till doomsday, Dr.

895
00:48:46.500 --> 00:48:49.600
Watson, with no effect at all.

896
00:48:50.240 --> 00:48:56.600
Still, it might make you a little
drowsy, like the white ribbon

897
00:48:56.680 --> 00:49:00.100
of road at night when you're driving.

898
00:49:00.700 --> 00:49:04.040
The rhythm is smooth,

899
00:49:04.500 --> 00:49:10.580
unbroken. And the road
goes on and on, round

900
00:49:10.660 --> 00:49:16.720
and round, always the same,
winding and winding.

901
00:49:17.060 --> 00:49:21.120
And you're drowsy, you're tired.

902
00:49:21.220 --> 00:49:25.280
Let the road come into you as it were.

903
00:49:25.440 --> 00:49:27.700
The long road,

904
00:49:27.980 --> 00:49:30.420
the smooth road,

905
00:49:30.660 --> 00:49:32.560
the road to sleep.

906
00:49:32.640 --> 00:49:33.640
Sleep.

907
00:49:34.600 --> 00:49:35.860
Sleep.

908
00:49:42.480 --> 00:49:44.220
Open your eyes.

909
00:49:45.040 --> 00:49:46.540
Stand up.

910
00:49:49.100 --> 00:49:50.640
Turn around.

911
00:49:52.280 --> 00:49:53.620
And now, Dr.

912
00:49:53.700 --> 00:49:56.580
Watson, you're on a holiday in Scotland.

913
00:49:56.800 --> 00:49:59.520
The country is amazingly beautiful.

914
00:49:59.600 --> 00:50:01.780
We're coming to a stream.

915
00:50:02.640 --> 00:50:04.480
It isn't deep.

916
00:50:05.680 --> 00:50:09.020
Better take your shoes and socks off.

917
00:50:19.080 --> 00:50:21.100
Roll up your trouser.

918
00:50:25.660 --> 00:50:28.740
That will do. The other leg is waterproof.

919
00:50:29.860 --> 00:50:31.380
Turn around.

920
00:50:38.820 --> 00:50:39.960
Sit down.

921
00:50:44.640 --> 00:50:45.960
Wake up now.

922
00:50:51.720 --> 00:50:53.380
There you are, you see?
What did I tell you?

923
00:50:53.460 --> 00:50:57.048
It didn't work with me. Why,
nobody with an ounce of carri...

924
00:51:02.720 --> 00:51:04.800
I think you'll need these.

925
00:51:10.640 --> 00:51:12.680
So, England, Alfred? Watson, she's here.

926
00:51:12.760 --> 00:51:14.340
Oh, woman you're looking for?

927
00:51:14.420 --> 00:51:15.900
Yes, I'm going to meet her.

928
00:51:15.980 --> 00:51:18.020
Perhaps I can induce her
to take me to Moriarty.

929
00:51:18.100 --> 00:51:19.220
Do you think it's wise, Holmes?

930
00:51:19.300 --> 00:51:21.340
May not be wise, but it's essential.

931
00:51:21.420 --> 00:51:23.300
After all, I've held me on
with Moriarty in the past.

932
00:51:23.380 --> 00:51:26.262
But isn't it dangerous?
She might be a hypnotist.

933
00:51:26.400 --> 00:51:26.900
I'm not stronger than hers.

934
00:51:26.960 --> 00:51:28.200
I deserve to be hypnotized.

935
00:51:28.280 --> 00:51:28.840
Shh.

936
00:51:28.920 --> 00:51:30.180
I feel I must protest, Dr.

937
00:51:30.260 --> 00:51:30.860
Onslow.

938
00:51:30.940 --> 00:51:34.140
I was told this was a gathering of
serious students of a great science.

939
00:51:34.220 --> 00:51:36.240
And I find myself in
a company of buffoons.

940
00:51:36.320 --> 00:51:37.540
Oh, my dear madam.

941
00:51:37.620 --> 00:51:39.040
Ellets and Esdell, brain.

942
00:51:39.120 --> 00:51:40.860
Were those men martyrs for the truth?

943
00:51:40.940 --> 00:51:43.100
That you made laugh over
your childish cruel tricks?

944
00:51:43.180 --> 00:51:45.160
I must say I'm in complete
agreement with you, madam.

945
00:51:45.240 --> 00:51:47.240
This was most unnecessary performance, Dr.

946
00:51:47.320 --> 00:51:49.120
Onslow. Beg your pardon, sir.

947
00:51:49.200 --> 00:51:51.160
My name is Holmes, Sherlock Holmes.

948
00:51:51.240 --> 00:51:52.420
At your service, madam.

949
00:51:52.500 --> 00:51:53.880
Thank you, Mr. Holmes.

950
00:51:53.960 --> 00:51:56.720
I'm afraid I've created a
rather embarrassing situation.

951
00:51:56.800 --> 00:51:59.200
But you see, I'm interested in
the serious study of hypnotism.

952
00:51:59.280 --> 00:52:00.300
So am I too.

953
00:52:00.580 --> 00:52:02.140
Perhaps we have something in common, Mr.

954
00:52:02.220 --> 00:52:03.380
Holmes. Perhaps we have.

955
00:52:03.460 --> 00:52:05.040
Would you join me for a
cocktail at Pembroke House?

956
00:52:05.120 --> 00:52:06.440
I should be delighted.

957
00:52:06.860 --> 00:52:07.860
Good.

958
00:52:21.540 --> 00:52:22.580
Thank you.

959
00:52:23.520 --> 00:52:25.120
It was such a pleasant place in London.

960
00:52:25.200 --> 00:52:27.260
It was so nice of you to
suggest our coming here.

961
00:52:27.340 --> 00:52:29.400
I thought a little picking
up would do us good.

962
00:52:29.480 --> 00:52:31.140
You mean you thought I looked...

963
00:52:31.220 --> 00:52:32.420
I like the way you look.

964
00:52:32.500 --> 00:52:33.580
Thank you.

965
00:52:36.620 --> 00:52:39.520
I suppose I did lose my head
a little at the Mesmer Club.

966
00:52:39.600 --> 00:52:42.920
But you see, hypnotism is
almost a religion with me.

967
00:52:43.100 --> 00:52:46.140
I know so well what it
can do to help and heal.

968
00:52:46.220 --> 00:52:48.700
And I can't bear to see it
used for trivial purposes.

969
00:52:48.780 --> 00:52:49.720
I know very little about it.

970
00:52:49.800 --> 00:52:50.740
That's why I went to the Mesmer Club.

971
00:52:50.820 --> 00:52:54.120
You see, I'm rather puzzled just now
with the case that I'm working on.

972
00:52:54.200 --> 00:52:55.580
How fascinating. Tell me about it.

973
00:52:55.660 --> 00:52:57.895
It's the murder of Sir George Fenwick.

974
00:52:58.880 --> 00:53:00.420
Fenwick? Who is he?

975
00:53:01.280 --> 00:53:02.840
Quite a well-known figure.

976
00:53:03.000 --> 00:53:04.820
Odd now, I come to think of it.

977
00:53:04.900 --> 00:53:08.312
The last time I saw Sir George
was here at Pembroke House.

978
00:53:08.560 --> 00:53:09.460
Strange.

979
00:53:09.540 --> 00:53:10.780
Yes, isn't it?

980
00:53:10.860 --> 00:53:13.520
He was sitting, um...

981
00:53:13.600 --> 00:53:16.188
I believe he was sitting
at this very table.

982
00:53:16.800 --> 00:53:17.800
Cigarette?

983
00:53:18.060 --> 00:53:19.460
Thanks. Do go on.

984
00:53:20.820 --> 00:53:21.840
I was a charming lady with him.

985
00:53:21.920 --> 00:53:24.700
He was, uh... he was lighting a cigarette.

986
00:53:30.560 --> 00:53:31.220
Charming.

987
00:53:31.300 --> 00:53:32.880
Did you see her face?

988
00:53:33.000 --> 00:53:34.260
No, it's not.

989
00:53:35.240 --> 00:53:36.600
Merely her back.

990
00:53:37.220 --> 00:53:38.620
How unenterprising of you.

991
00:53:38.700 --> 00:53:39.920
Yes, wasn't it?

992
00:53:40.000 --> 00:53:41.520
I'm afraid I'm getting a little older.

993
00:53:41.600 --> 00:53:43.040
I shouldn't say so.

994
00:53:43.120 --> 00:53:44.020
That's nice of you.

995
00:53:44.100 --> 00:53:45.100
Still,

996
00:53:45.500 --> 00:53:48.180
the first time in my life I've got
hold of a case that's beyond me.

997
00:53:48.260 --> 00:53:50.640
I'm actually losing sleep over it.

998
00:53:50.720 --> 00:53:53.620
You know, Mr. Holmes,
I believe I could help you.

999
00:53:54.020 --> 00:53:55.980
Really? I should be very grateful.

1000
00:53:56.060 --> 00:53:57.440
You're amused.

1001
00:53:57.560 --> 00:53:59.380
Oh, nearly skeptical.

1002
00:53:59.500 --> 00:54:01.029
How would you go about it?

1003
00:54:01.540 --> 00:54:04.246
I've used hypnotism more
than once in healing.

1004
00:54:04.520 --> 00:54:05.600
Not for profit.

1005
00:54:05.680 --> 00:54:07.140
I'm not a professional.

1006
00:54:07.320 --> 00:54:09.280
But I do think I could help you.

1007
00:54:09.620 --> 00:54:11.220
If you'd care to...

1008
00:54:11.300 --> 00:54:13.712
I can't think of a pleasanter experience.

1009
00:54:28.960 --> 00:54:31.220
Low lights, music,
is that all there is to it?

1010
00:54:31.300 --> 00:54:32.780
You must relax, Mr. Holmes.

1011
00:54:32.860 --> 00:54:35.507
I'm afraid you're a
rather difficult subject.

1012
00:54:38.440 --> 00:54:40.660
So I thought perhaps a little help.

1013
00:54:42.720 --> 00:54:44.740
Materia medica might be advisable.

1014
00:54:45.120 --> 00:54:46.120
Drugs?

1015
00:54:50.280 --> 00:54:52.180
No, I'd rather not if you don't mind.

1016
00:54:52.260 --> 00:54:54.840
As a matter of fact,
I'd rather not myself.

1017
00:54:55.080 --> 00:54:58.198
But Schrenk-Natzin,
he practiced in Munich, you know.

1018
00:55:00.400 --> 00:55:01.580
Do you mind?

1019
00:55:01.980 --> 00:55:04.680
Well, as a matter of fact,
I don't approve of sedatives.

1020
00:55:04.760 --> 00:55:05.960
Just as you wish.

1021
00:55:06.040 --> 00:55:08.160
We don't have to go on
with this at all, you know.

1022
00:55:08.240 --> 00:55:09.240
Wait a minute.

1023
00:55:11.880 --> 00:55:12.940
Wait a minute.

1024
00:55:16.320 --> 00:55:17.340
All right.

1025
00:55:17.420 --> 00:55:18.500
I'll take a chance.

1026
00:55:18.580 --> 00:55:20.180
It's really quite harmless.

1027
00:55:20.880 --> 00:55:21.980
What is it?

1028
00:55:22.320 --> 00:55:24.420
Cannabis japonica, an oriental soporific.

1029
00:55:24.500 --> 00:55:25.760
You need water.

1030
00:55:38.560 --> 00:55:39.740
Thank you.

1031
00:55:43.240 --> 00:55:45.200
Now sit down, Mr. Hobbs.

1032
00:55:49.220 --> 00:55:51.540
You'll feel yourself growing drowsy.

1033
00:55:51.880 --> 00:55:53.380
Don't fight it.

1034
00:55:53.500 --> 00:55:55.000
Give in to it.

1035
00:55:55.520 --> 00:55:57.840
Because you do want to sleep, you know.

1036
00:55:59.940 --> 00:56:03.540
Just fix your eyes on
this one white flower...

1037
00:56:04.840 --> 00:56:07.040
floating on the water...

1038
00:56:08.540 --> 00:56:11.100
to your mind of every other thought.

1039
00:56:12.240 --> 00:56:14.400
Follow the motion of the water.

1040
00:56:14.820 --> 00:56:16.540
So smooth.

1041
00:56:17.200 --> 00:56:18.760
Not a ripple.

1042
00:56:19.920 --> 00:56:22.260
Waters of forgetfulness.

1043
00:56:24.500 --> 00:56:25.800
Steady.

1044
00:56:27.240 --> 00:56:28.540
Deep.

1045
00:56:30.320 --> 00:56:31.620
Strong.

1046
00:56:33.480 --> 00:56:35.340
Strange, isn't it?

1047
00:56:35.420 --> 00:56:37.560
How the light is reflected.

1048
00:56:38.540 --> 00:56:43.120
Little specks of light that move and move.

1049
00:56:47.100 --> 00:56:49.500
It's restful here.

1050
00:56:51.420 --> 00:56:53.000
It's peaceful.

1051
00:56:55.480 --> 00:56:57.480
It's friendly.

1052
00:56:58.460 --> 00:57:02.200
And you're very close to
finding what you're looking for.

1053
00:57:03.260 --> 00:57:05.460
You'll find them soon now.

1054
00:57:05.820 --> 00:57:07.640
The guilty ones.

1055
00:57:09.140 --> 00:57:15.260
When you're rested,
gentle waters closing over

1056
00:57:15.340 --> 00:57:16.340
you.

1057
00:57:16.920 --> 00:57:18.820
Steady,

1058
00:57:19.400 --> 00:57:21.020
deep,

1059
00:57:21.740 --> 00:57:23.400
strong.

1060
00:57:25.040 --> 00:57:27.800
Drawing you down.

1061
00:57:29.120 --> 00:57:31.020
Down.

1062
00:57:32.400 --> 00:57:34.040
Down.

1063
00:57:42.300 --> 00:57:44.200
Sleep.

1064
00:57:46.300 --> 00:57:47.580
Sleep.

1065
00:58:15.540 --> 00:58:18.840
I'm sorry.

1066
00:58:42.300 --> 00:58:44.320
Here he is, Professor Moriarty.

1067
00:58:45.960 --> 00:58:47.800
Stand up, Mr. Holmes.

1068
00:58:52.800 --> 00:58:54.520
Open your eyes.

1069
00:58:56.320 --> 00:58:57.880
Face this way.

1070
00:59:01.700 --> 00:59:03.180
Are you satisfied?

1071
00:59:05.060 --> 00:59:06.920
We are dealing with a clever man.

1072
00:59:07.000 --> 00:59:08.480
He may be shamming.

1073
00:59:09.080 --> 00:59:13.220
There's just one infallible
test for profound hypnosis.

1074
00:59:13.780 --> 00:59:15.600
You ready, Dr. Simnor?

1075
00:59:26.100 --> 00:59:27.760
That will do, Doctor.

1076
00:59:27.980 --> 00:59:30.568
He couldn't fake
insensibility to the knife.

1077
00:59:31.320 --> 00:59:33.420
I congratulate you, Lydia.

1078
00:59:34.780 --> 00:59:36.620
Turn around, Mr. Holmes.

1079
00:59:38.080 --> 00:59:40.120
Now walk to the desk.

1080
00:59:46.440 --> 00:59:47.820
Sit down.

1081
00:59:48.880 --> 00:59:52.680
Take that pen, and write
what I tell you to write.

1082
00:59:53.120 --> 00:59:56.180
I have at last found a
case which I cannot solve.

1083
01:00:00.860 --> 01:00:03.360
I have outlived my usefulness.

1084
01:00:07.060 --> 01:00:10.200
Therefore I have decided to end my life.

1085
01:00:15.200 --> 01:00:16.740
Sign your name.

1086
01:00:19.300 --> 01:00:20.760
Now blot it.

1087
01:00:25.840 --> 01:00:27.260
Fold it up.

1088
01:00:29.380 --> 01:00:31.200
And put it in your pocket.

1089
01:00:32.320 --> 01:00:33.720
Comes to Sherlock Holmes.

1090
01:00:33.800 --> 01:00:35.094
I'm sorry, Mr. Holmes.

1091
01:00:35.420 --> 01:00:37.240
Go out onto the terrace.

1092
01:00:39.140 --> 01:00:41.320
But it won't look like suicide, sir.

1093
01:00:41.400 --> 01:00:45.106
I'm sorry, but Mr. Holmes'
injuries must all be self-inflicted.

1094
01:00:47.160 --> 01:00:49.180
Let's walk a little, Mr. Holmes.

1095
01:00:50.720 --> 01:00:53.580
It's so pleasant here in the garden.

1096
01:00:56.720 --> 01:00:59.260
Just step up here onto the terrace.

1097
01:00:59.340 --> 01:01:01.340
It's a nice, broad terrace.

1098
01:01:04.320 --> 01:01:08.500
Now turn to the left and walk
slowly to the end of the terrace.

1099
01:01:21.360 --> 01:01:24.280
Don't stop. You must
walk to the end, you know.

1100
01:01:28.500 --> 01:01:30.660
The end leads to an open doorway.

1101
01:01:30.740 --> 01:01:33.211
You can pass through it in perfect safety.

1102
01:01:33.800 --> 01:01:36.620
beyond the doorway, you'll find
what you've been looking for.

1103
01:01:36.700 --> 01:01:38.220
Must you drag this on?

1104
01:01:38.300 --> 01:01:40.920
This is the moment I've been
anticipating for a long time,

1105
01:01:41.000 --> 01:01:41.740
my dear.

1106
01:01:41.820 --> 01:01:43.640
Go on, Mr. Holmes.

1107
01:01:48.800 --> 01:01:52.900
Through the open doorway, you will find
the man responsible for the finger murders

1108
01:01:52.980 --> 01:01:55.240
and the death of Sir George Fenwick.

1109
01:01:55.960 --> 01:01:57.440
Professor Moriarty.

1110
01:01:57.520 --> 01:01:58.540
Holmes!

1111
01:02:00.080 --> 01:02:01.360
Stand still!

1112
01:02:02.660 --> 01:02:03.900
What a beautiful view, Watson.

1113
01:02:03.980 --> 01:02:05.860
I'm quite enjoying it. No, you're not.

1114
01:02:05.940 --> 01:02:07.280
You're hypnotized.

1115
01:02:07.360 --> 01:02:08.680
You're under a spell.

1116
01:02:08.800 --> 01:02:10.480
Stand still. Don't move.

1117
01:02:10.560 --> 01:02:12.020
Sidney Holmes, Sidney does it.

1118
01:02:12.100 --> 01:02:13.520
Stand perfectly still where you are.

1119
01:02:13.600 --> 01:02:14.740
Nonsense, Watson.

1120
01:02:14.820 --> 01:02:16.120
You don't know what you're doing.

1121
01:02:16.200 --> 01:02:17.360
Of course I know what I'm doing.

1122
01:02:17.440 --> 01:02:18.600
You mean you're not hypnotized?

1123
01:02:18.680 --> 01:02:19.600
Certainly not.

1124
01:02:19.680 --> 01:02:21.621
Then get off the wall, you idiot.

1125
01:02:24.580 --> 01:02:26.380
What were you doing up there?

1126
01:02:26.460 --> 01:02:27.940
Holding the fort until you arrived.

1127
01:02:28.020 --> 01:02:31.800
What kept you? I ran into a spot of
trouble on my way to Scotland Yard.

1128
01:02:31.880 --> 01:02:34.220
I was arrested for
proceeding the speed limit.

1129
01:02:34.300 --> 01:02:35.520
Your luck seems to hold, Mr.

1130
01:02:35.600 --> 01:02:36.600
Holmes.

1131
01:02:36.680 --> 01:02:38.260
I'd hardly call it luck, Professor.

1132
01:02:38.340 --> 01:02:41.740
You see, I substituted a drug of my own
for the one that this dear lady pressed on

1133
01:02:41.820 --> 01:02:42.520
me.

1134
01:02:42.600 --> 01:02:44.160
You are clever, aren't you?

1135
01:02:44.240 --> 01:02:47.720
A drug that, although it leaves the subject
conscious, renders him quite insensitive

1136
01:02:47.800 --> 01:02:51.040
to pain. That accounted for
my lack of reaction to Dr.

1137
01:02:51.120 --> 01:02:52.180
Simrel's knife.

1138
01:02:52.600 --> 01:02:54.953
Well, Gregson, quite an impressive haul.

1139
01:02:55.060 --> 01:02:57.480
Even Inspector Lestrade himself
couldn't have done any better.

1140
01:02:57.560 --> 01:02:58.760
Thanks, Mr. Hall.

1141
01:03:02.420 --> 01:03:04.240
I was right, Mr. Holmes.

1142
01:03:04.320 --> 01:03:06.100
You are a difficult subject.

1143
01:03:06.180 --> 01:03:07.220
Thank you.

1144
01:03:09.880 --> 01:03:11.420
And now, Professor,

1145
01:03:11.920 --> 01:03:13.760
our score is settled.

1146
01:03:14.280 --> 01:03:15.960
Au revoir, until I see you on the gallows.

1147
01:03:16.040 --> 01:03:18.160
The rope has not been made
that'll go around my neck.

1148
01:03:18.240 --> 01:03:19.240
Come on.

1149
01:03:32.180 --> 01:03:33.420
I'll take care of things, Mr.

1150
01:03:33.500 --> 01:03:34.640
Holmes. Thank you, Inspector.

1151
01:03:34.720 --> 01:03:35.720
Come on.

1152
01:03:37.380 --> 01:03:40.400
An evil man, Holmes,
but what a horrible death.

1153
01:03:40.480 --> 01:03:41.892
Better than he deserved.

1154
01:03:43.920 --> 01:03:45.391
What are you thinking of?

1155
01:03:45.780 --> 01:03:48.720
I'm thinking of all the women who can come
and go in safety in the streets of London

1156
01:03:48.800 --> 01:03:49.800
tonight.

1157
01:03:51.160 --> 01:03:53.395
The stars keep watching their heavens.

1158
01:03:54.320 --> 01:03:59.144
And in our own little way, we too, old
friend, a privilege to watch over our city.

